Subject: ksud: ask Zygisk Next for its injection state
Upstream-Status: Pending [SukiSU-Ultra main]
Drop-when: upstream detects Zygisk Next without relying on its process name

Zygisk Next can hide its daemon's process name, so the process scan
reported it as not running. Run its zygiskd status command (killed
after 2 s) and require exactly one inject_state:1 line. NeoZygisk and
NyaZygisk keep the process-name check.
---
diff --git a/userspace/ksud/src/module.rs b/userspace/ksud/src/module.rs
index c04d49074d4e133b2d62fb3837388e77d9b715ff..7b90dbb1f3adcdea7c1cf12b32082b031d19e2be 100644
--- a/userspace/ksud/src/module.rs
+++ b/userspace/ksud/src/module.rs
@@ -1069,12 +1069,40 @@ where
     false
 }
 
-/// Determine whether the Zygisk provider's daemon is actually running
+/// Query Zygisk Next directly because its daemon can hide its process name.
+fn is_zygisk_next_running() -> bool {
+    let Ok(output) = Command::new(assets::BUSYBOX_PATH)
+        .args([
+            "timeout",
+            "-s",
+            "KILL",
+            "2",
+            "/data/adb/modules/zygisksu/bin/zygiskd",
+            "status",
+        ])
+        .output()
+    else {
+        return false;
+    };
+    if !output.status.success() {
+        return false;
+    }
+    let Ok(status) = std::str::from_utf8(&output.stdout) else {
+        return false;
+    };
+    let mut states = status
+        .lines()
+        .filter_map(|line| line.strip_prefix("inject_state:"));
+    matches!((states.next(), states.next()), (Some("1"), None))
+}
+
